WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.340
It was the morning of my departure
on a one-day business trip to Osaka.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.920
What's our plan... for the marriage ceremony?

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.370
Wh-where did that come from all of a sudden?

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.710
We're not going to get married.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.880
Oh shit! I'm going to be late!

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:30.130
Um... s-sorry! Let's talk about this later!

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.500
I'm going to be late
for the Shinkansen so I'm leaving now.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:35.580
Sorry!

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:38.800
Huh?

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:03.010
A man who can work, that's the type she likes

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.300
I psyched myself up and got down to business

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.870
But I'm always so busy and so bored

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.540
The company I work at now is pretty high level

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.710
And my dad has a lot of connections there

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.870
So there's no way I can quit

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:39.290
I'm always all by myself

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:44.460
I just take a bath and fall asleep

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.880
I can't even take the time to admire

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:56.340
Your hair or the way you walk

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.630
If all I can do is sleep

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:07.880
Then at least in my dreams

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.920
I want to see you

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.910
Princess Man

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.710
Now that I think about it... what he said...

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.210
What's our plan... for the marriage ceremony?

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.580
He... he wasn't proposing to me...

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.250
He was talking about Kuraki-kun's marriage
ceremony that we're attending next month!

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:56.000
I mean, we've been dating for 4 years now...
so of course I'd react to the "M" word.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.800
I was also surprised because
we generally don't talk about things like that.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.500
But why did I go and blurt out
"We're not going to"...?

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.880
Was that just a Freudian slip...?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.080
I wonder if I'm even suited to become a bride...

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.760
I've been so focused on work that
I've never taken time to even think about it.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.590
Though, it's not as if I don't want to get married.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.960
In fact, I want to, if it's possible.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.630
Someday.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.210
But, all the necessary prep...

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.540
And lifestyle changes...

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:39.170
When I think about those, I feel reluctant.
And that makes me wonder if I'll ever be ready...

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.880
As a woman, isn't that a bad sign?

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.420
Welcome back, Senpai.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.300
All the way to Osaka and back
in one day is exhausting...

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.080
Why didn't you just head straight home?

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.580
Well... I have an article to write.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.330
And materials to prepare for an interview.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.050
I wonder if I'll even make it home tonight...

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.090
Ah... what a wonderful smell!

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.670
What is this?

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.800
Isn't it Yumi-san's perfume?

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:13.760
I wonder why... it's like the smell of happiness itself.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.380
Oh, that's right!

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.420
Yumi-san got engaged!

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.290
Huh?

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:19.290
Engaged?!

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.170
Right, Yumi-san?

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:21.790
Huh?

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.620
That's great! Congratulations on your engagement!

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.880
Thank you.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.670
I see... then it really is the smell of happiness.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.670
Oh... are you going home already, Yumi-chan?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.540
Yes. I have a special meeting with Shimura
the baseball player tomorrow.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.630
So... please excuse me for today.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.500
According to Kobu-chan's network of sources...

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.080
Yumi-san's finance was actually...
stolen from another woman!

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.510
Stolen from another woman?

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:53.420
Apparently, the fiance was already
set to marry his girlfriend of 8 years,

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:56.420
but then he broke up with her
and got engaged to Yumi-san instead!

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.790
Oh?

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.670
Stole a man, huh?

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.590
Not the other way around...

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.830
As a woman, I want to learn from her!

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.620
What's wrong?

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.210
Yumi-chan... already left, right?

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:13.130
I think so.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.210
Why do you ask?

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.330
I wanted to ask her a favor...

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.630
I totally forgot.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.580
Yumi-chan's
Bleacher Report

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.550
Yumi-chan writes a popular column.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:30.080
She closely follows the career of Junji Shimura, a
young superstar in the Japanese Baseball League.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.960
He hates interviews and makes reporters cry,
but he took a liking to her.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.420
So she was allowed to write the column.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.090
"Yumi-chan won him over with her good looks."

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.710
That's the dominant rumor at the office...
Is there anything you're focusing on in your training now?

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:54.000
Which is why, well, they probably have
THAT kind of relationship.
Doing longer runs, I suppose.
I've been working on those every day.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:57.000
Must be nice to be a woman!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.540
All they have to do to get a good article
is sleep with somebody.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:04.670
Normally sports coverage is so competitive,
a magazine like ours would never stand a chance.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.710
But she gets "close coverage"...
I wonder just how close she actually gets!

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:09.590
Close in bed!

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:11.920
Don't worry about it.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.090
But, Senpai...!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.380
Oh yeah, it must be so great to score a job
just by getting in bed.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.340
Well, I doubt anybody's lining up
for a shot with you.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:27.830
Out of the 40 staff in the editorial department,
there are only 4 women...

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:31.250
No matter what, there's always
some asshole spouting crap like this.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.840
Even so, it still pisses me off!

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.710
You blame everyone else
for your own damn failures,

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.880
which is why your articles
always end up being shit!

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:53.080
SAY THAT AGAIN, I DARE YOU!

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:56.250
Dojima-san!

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.670
Calm down for a second, Dojima-san!

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.120
Please just hold it back!

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.540
Let's just go outside and cool off!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:14.460
When you said "Don't worry about it"...
I thought that meant to ignore him!

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.710
You are seriously scary sometimes, Senpai!

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.210
I intended to just let it go, but...

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.630
Dojima-san never lets anything go,
so please be careful out there.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.210
Seriously...

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.580
I can't believe I did something so stupid!

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:35.670
Is this guy really that incompetent at his job?

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:42.340
Rather than incompetent, I'd just say...
he's not the type cut out for a weekly magazine.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:47.590
I see what you're going for,
but you're emphasizing the point way too strongly.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.750
Why don't you try writing it again
with more of a softer tone?

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.630
Dojima-san has always been
a sarcastic person, anyways.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.040
But...

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.460
Even though I knew that, in that one instant
I just kind of... blew my top.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.420
Regardless of your intent...

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:09.870
Being told off by a 20-something-year-old woman
in front of everyone almost certainly hurt his pride.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.590
I know, right...

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:16.040
I really wish... I could just take it all back.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:20.370
On top of that... who was the girl, um,
that you said stole a husband?

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.370
Ah... you mean Yumi-chan.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:26.620
Yeah, about Yumi-chan...
what's the real story there?

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.460
As far as you know, it is THAT
kind of relationship isn't it?

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.840
Well... yeah, that's true.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:41.370
That's right... she actually could
be sleeping with him.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:45.670
Gotansha Publishing

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:48.870
Good morning!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.840
She's just the absolute worse, you can't find
a woman who's more bitchy! Honestly!

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:59.290
If you become like Matsukata,
then there's not a man alive who would touch you.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.630
He's talking about me...

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:05.790
Yumi-chan...?

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.500
Nobody would ever think
about marrying that kind of crazy!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.380
So Yumi-chan, don't ever start
taking after someone like her.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.420
Okay, I'll be careful!

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.380
Even though I was partly in the wrong,
it still really hurts to suffer the aftermath.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.130
I didn't get angry at him
for Yumi-chan's sake or anything, but...

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:31.630
"I'll be careful!"... Is that really the best reaction
she should could come up with?

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.880
Good morning.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:35.840
Good morning.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:40.920
Um... Matsukata-san, I heard
that you wanted to talk with me?

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.880
Ah, that's right!

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.920
I had a favor to ask regarding one
of the articles I'm currently working on.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.380
Work is work.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.210
I have to leave my feelings out of it.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:54.050
I'd really love it if you
could get me an interview with Shimura.

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:56.920
Would you mind introducing me to him, Yumi-chan?

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:01.000
Introducing... you?

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.580
Huh? Is that not okay?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:10.620
Well, if I could just go along with you to one of his
practice sessions then I'll handle the rest myself.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.500
Do you have a copy of your pitch I could look at?

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.830
Oh... sure. Of course.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.000
Pitch
The Seven Samurai

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:23.300
If you just want me to give this to him,
then that's fine.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:27.420
But Shimura only does interviews
with people he's cleared ahead of time.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.000
Which is exactly why I'm asking you
to help me get an in!

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:33.420
Then, if you could just give that to him
it would really help. Please.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.170
Alright.

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:36.250
Thanks.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:38.300
Um... sorry.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.790
I didn't mean to put you in a tough situa...tion...

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.580
Is she trying to say that Shimura belongs to her?

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.300
Don't think you can just monopolize him!

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:08.840
This is a job!

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.670
Don't pretend...

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:16.630
...you're some kind of princess!

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:28.380
Yumi Nogawa (26)
Occupation: Magazine Editor

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.830
"I'm a working woman who needs no man!"

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.250
I don't get along with people like that.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.040
Sexual harassment?

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:34.000
If it helps to get me more work as a woman
in this business, then why make it an issue?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.870
I think denying that advantage
is not only unnatural, but unattractive.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.710
"The Seven Samurai"...?

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:49.590
What's that?

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.460
This is the pitch.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:56.590
"Japanese people making their way abroad"?

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:58.960
Are you sure this was meant for me?

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:03.380
Do they think I'm going
to the major leagues or something?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:12.090
I've covered six of the modern day "samurai"...

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:13.670
Just one left.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.210
THE SAMURAI SPIRIT!!
Junji Shimura
Triple Play
Comback
Victory!

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.960
Shimura the baseball player.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:21.500
What?!

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:22.630
He won't do it?!

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:23.880
Yeah.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.170
Shimura isn't interested in doing
an interview for "The Seven Samurai."

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:29.130
No way...

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.500
Did you explain the main point of the article?

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.630
I showed him your pitch.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.500
I wanted you to do more than just show it to him...

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.920
I only agreed to show him the pitch that you wrote.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:44.370
Even if that's true, you know how pointless it is
unless you explain the gist of the article first.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:49.580
I can't do that. The amount of time he has
for interviews after practice is limited.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.630
There are other reporters, too.
Our company doesn't get any special treatment.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:58.250
We're both writers for the same magazine,
so why can't you be more cooperative?

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:02.080
If you always make it so personal...
people start to assume things, you know.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:07.500
The same applies to you, Matsukata-san.
Please don't let your jealousy get the better of you.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.580
Jealousy?!

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:10.960
You're one to talk!

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:14.080
I think I've been more than cooperative with you.

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.710
Ah, wait!

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:16.760
You dropped something-

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:18.960
Wait, this is...

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.420
Pitch
The Seven Samurai

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.380
This is my pitch!

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:26.540
I thought you were a nice girl,
so I tried to be modest, but this is...!

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:28.170
Damn it!

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:41.050
Shimura was so focused during today's game!
I was drawn in and put on the edge of my seat!

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.540
I don't get why this column is so popular...

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.420
That's rare to see.

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:48.340
Dojima-san's pitch got accepted.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:51.250
Oh... that's right!

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:55.170
From what I hear, he's working on something about
the illegal dumping problem going around lately.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:56.880
But that's...!

00:13:58.460 --> 00:13:59.460
Senpai?

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.460
Narita-san!

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.710
Is it true about Dojima-san's pitch?

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.630
Oh... yeah.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:09.790
You submitted one too, right? On the same topic.

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:11.550
So why did Dojima-san...?

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.960
He submitted a pitch too, similar to yours.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:15.870
Huh?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:21.210
That being said, the pitch he submitted was written
from a different perspective than yours.

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:24.580
In the end, we decided
to go with Dojima's take on it.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:33.790
I see... although we wrote on the same subject,
he came at the problem in a way I didn't think of.

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.120
Well, don't worry about it.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:40.000
You've got other work to do, right?

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.960
How's that one coming, "The Seven Samurai"?

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:45.880
I just need to complete an interview
with one last subject.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:48.250
I see. Keep it up.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:55.500
Oh? You sure have unique ideas
for your articles, Dojima-san.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.910
Well, you know... those idiots
who only think inside the box all the time

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:05.130
always write shallow articles
that could never compare to my work. Never.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:08.420
Oh?

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:09.960
What's this?

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.500
"The Seven Samurai"?

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:19.170
I can tell already... another trite piece of crap
like that article on the foreign affairs minister.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:22.300
All showy on the outside,
but has no real substance to it at all.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:27.210
I mean, who even writes a pitch this long?
Did they even think about who has to read it?!

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:31.420
The amount of time he has
for interviews after practice is limited.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:37.000
Well... writers who come up with this stuff always-

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:44.130
What?

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:56.290
Wh-what is her deal?

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:14.250
So I'll go beyond the night and meet with you

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:18.210
Let all of the sadness come to an end tonight

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:18.960
The amount of time he has
for interviews after practice is limited.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:23.210
Raise that singing voice and let it reach me now

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.250
That's right... with a limited amount
of time for interviews,

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:25.710
I got rock'n roll music

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.500
there's no chance he'd read this entire pitch.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.170
Rock'n roll music

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:28.880
But...

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:32.050
So Yumi-chan, don't ever start
taking after someone like her.

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:34.250
Okay, I'll be careful!

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:38.540
Shimura only does interviews
with people he's cleared ahead of time.

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:44.040
I thought I had thrown away all of my memories

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:43.290
The same applies to you, Matsukata-san.
Please don't let your jealousy get the better of you.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:45.620
Wh-where does she get off?!

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:51.500
Yet I somehow remembered that and laughed slyly

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:49.000
This is exactly why I hate
having to work with women!

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.170
Then... does that make me a man?

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:58.290
I'm sure that I will not know true love yet

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:53.580
No.

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:55.670
I'm a woman.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:57.620
A woman who fights!

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:03.380
An interview with Shimura... I'll make it happen!

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:22.830
Is he here?

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:25.300
What's up with her?

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.290
Why is a weekly reporter here?

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:28.210
Don't just wander around.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.160
You're getting in the way!

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:31.750
It was quite scary.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.750
At first I couldn't make my way
through the crowd at all.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:41.380
But at some point, I realized they act so rough
because they don't want to lose to the other guys.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:44.550
So I simply stopped using force.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.420
If I acted more feminine,
I figured they would treat me more like a lady.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:55.330
Once I started playing the caring young lady role,
they became much more receptive and kind to me.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:59.500
Oh... Shimura just came out!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.830
It's worse than I thought...
So combative and no holes in their defense.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.210
It's like a war...

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.170
You can't fight the wave.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:16.550
You must avoid it.

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:21.910
Yumi-chan...

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.460
Within a herd of tanned men...

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.920
One person carries the floral scent of freesias...

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.050
She is a female Hataraki Man.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.460
Excuse me, Shimura!

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.250
Excuse me for interrupting.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.040
I'm Matsukata with Weekly JIDAI.

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:53.420
As a pro, instead of going abroad, you've tried
to bring Japanese baseball to the world's attention.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:56.250
I believe that attitude exemplifies
a modern day samurai.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.460
That is the focus of my article.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:03.000
Ah... this is that pitch someone brought up before.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.620
So, that's what it was about.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.960
Please, allow me to interview you.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:13.710
I...

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.500
can never turn down a request from a lady.

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:19.130
I did it!

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:25.250
Junji Shimura (29)
Pro Baseball Player - Infielder

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:25.250
Yes... Nogawa-san really has an eye for detail.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:26.750
Junji Shimura
Professional Record

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.250
Always tracking my condition...

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:31.800
And that time she showed me
the scrapbook of articles

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.460
dating back to my high school championship?

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:35.580
I got pretty emotional.

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:39.460
Of course, now she's one of
the few reporters who I can really trust.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:42.050
Thank you.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:45.960
And I... owe you an apology.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:48.170
It's okay.

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:52.290
I also owe you... some gratitude, Matsukata-san.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.250
Huh?

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:57.210
I heard that Dojima-san said
some really terrible things about me.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:59.090
And you got angry at him on my behalf, right?

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.410
Oh... yeah.

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:02.800
That made me happy.

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:06.460
In my experience, it's rare for other women
to treat me as an ally.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:13.080
But... after that happened, you looked like you
were getting along with Dojima-san.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:17.670
Even if we get seriously upset at them, they just
make life harder for us later, don't you think?

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:18.960
Those type of people.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.800
We should just let them fawn over us instead.

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:29.590
Yumi-chan... got married two months later.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.300
All the old men of the office took it pretty hard.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:02.170
I ended up catching the bride's bouquet, but...

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.000
I still haven't been proposed to.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:07.500
But that's okay.

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:11.630
Special Feature
The Seven Samurai
Junji Shimura:
"I owe everything
to that person"

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:12.000
Just maybe, my dream
isn't to become a bride at an altar.

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:17.710
But rather to use my pen like a katana and
continue to fight... as the eighth modern samurai.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.380
Shangri-la

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:37.590
Even in my dreams you can't manage a proper smile

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:42.910
I just want to chide and love a hopeless person like you

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:49.920
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:53.500
Where shall we go?

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:58.960
Ahh... ahh...

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:02.210
Shangri-la

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:06.170
Let me hear you shout "I'm happy!"

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:10.460
Let me see the tears underneath your tough exterior

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:12.130
Shangri-la

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:17.090
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:22.120
Please chide and love a hopeless person like me

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:25.380
Shinji
Nice Work Today
Do your best, but don't
wear yourself out.
-Shinji

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:35.710
Next Episode: Meticulous Man
